"WILDWOOD FLOWER"I WILL MINGLE MY TRESSESOF RAVEN BLACK HAIRWITH THE ROSES SO REDAND THE LILIES SO FAIR,WITH THE MYRTLE AS BRIGHTAS THE EMERALD DEW,THE GHOSTLY PALE RIDERWITH EYES OF BRIGHT BLUE.OH, HE TAUGHT ME TO LOVE HIMAND CALLED ME HIS FLOW'RA BRIGHT BLOSSOM TO CHEERHIM THROUGH LIFE'S WEARY HOUR,HOW MY HEART IS NOW WON-D'RING NO MIS'RY CAN TELL,HE LEFT WITH NO WARNINGNO WORD OF FAREWELL.I WILL DANCE, I WILL SING ANDMY HEART WILL BE GAY,I WILL CHARM EV'RY HEARTAND DRIVE TROUBLES AWAY,I HAVE WOKE FROM MY DREAMAND MY IDOL IS CLAYALL PORTIONS OF LOVEHAVE FLOWN FAR AWAY. 